      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 After section 49E of the Principal Act the following section is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.5",
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"49EA. (1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n49E (2), extend the period of operation of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on subsection 49E (2) in the same way as they\napply to the making of a restraining order.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional",
      "skos:definition": "inserted:\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"49EA. (1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n49E (2), extend the period of operation of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on subsection 49E (2) in the same way as they\napply to the making of a restraining order.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-8-logic-diffusion-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d981be9a90b006bb68d0b0fe80d8bb6b68486d9a7b33881d18edd6af965798e9",
      "skos:note": "The court may extend a restraining order made in reliance on subsection 49E (2) with the necessary changes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 After section 49E of the Principal Act the following section is",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 5,
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"49EA. (1) Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n49E (2), extend the period of operation of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 49D(1), (2), (3) and (5) apply, with the necessary\nchanges made, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining\norder made in reliance on subsection 49E (2) in the same way as they\napply to the making of a restraining order.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of a restraining order to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional"
    },
    {
