    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Section 12",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "Section 16 of the Principal Act is amended: .\n(a) by omitting from subsection (5) everything after \"in relation\nto\" and substituting:\n\"any action by the cash dealer or person taken:\n(c) under this section; or\n(d) in the mistaken belief that such action was required\nunder this section.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n(b) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsections:\n\"(5A) Where a cash dealer communicates to the Director,\nunder subsection (1), information about the cash dealer's\nsuspicion in relation to a transaction to which the cash dealer\nis a party, the cash dealer must not, unless required to do so\nunder this Act or any other Act, disclose to anyone else:\n(a) that the cash dealer has formed the suspicion; or\n(b) that information has been communicated to the Director;\nor\n(c) any other information from which the person to whom\nthe information is disclosed could reasonably be expected\nto infer that the suspicion had been formed or that the\nfirst-mentioned information had been communicated.\n\"(5B) A cash dealer who contravenes subsection (5A) is guilty\nof an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding\n$5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years, or\nboth.\n\"(5C) Subsection (5A) does not prevent a cash dealer from\ncommunicating or disclosing to any court any information, or\nmatter, referred to in that subsection.\".",
      "skos:definition": "Section 16 of the Principal Act is amended: .\n(a) by omitting from subsection (5) everything after \"in relation\nto\" and substituting:\n\"any action by the cash dealer or person taken:\n(c) under this section; or\n(d) in the mistaken belief that such action was required\nunder this section.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n(b) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsections:\n\"(5A) Where a cash dealer communicates to the Director,\nunder subsection (1), information about the cash dealer's\nsuspicion in relation to a transaction to which the cash dealer\nis a party, the cash dealer must not, unless required to do so\nunder this Act or any other Act, disclose to anyone else:\n(a) that the cash dealer has formed the suspicion; or\n(b) that information has been communicated to the Director;\nor\n(c) any other information from which the person to whom\nthe information is disclosed could reasonably be expected\nto infer that the suspicion had been formed or that the\nfirst-mentioned information had been communicated.\n\"(5B) A cash dealer who contravenes subsection (5A) is guilty\nof an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding\n$5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years, or\nboth.\n\"(5C) Subsection (5A) does not prevent a cash dealer from\ncommunicating or disclosing to any court any information, or\nmatter, referred to in that subsection.\".",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-12-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "33c7c957b5a463b5dd8c31f18ffb1cfa2edb2de8eb5c9f41714a31ec03937586",
      "skos:note": "Cash dealer must not disclose suspicion information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 Section 12",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "Section 16 of the Principal Act is amended: .\n(a) by omitting from subsection (5) everything after \"in relation\nto\" and substituting:\n\"any action by the cash dealer or person taken:\n(c) under this section; or\n(d) in the mistaken belief that such action was required\nunder this section.\";\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n(b) by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsections:\n\"(5A) Where a cash dealer communicates to the Director,\nunder subsection (1), information about the cash dealer's\nsuspicion in relation to a transaction to which the cash dealer\nis a party, the cash dealer must not, unless required to do so\nunder this Act or any other Act, disclose to anyone else:\n(a) that the cash dealer has formed the suspicion; or\n(b) that information has been communicated to the Director;\nor\n(c) any other information from which the person to whom\nthe information is disclosed could reasonably be expected\nto infer that the suspicion had been formed or that the\nfirst-mentioned information had been communicated.\n\"(5B) A cash dealer who contravenes subsection (5A) is guilty\nof an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding\n$5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years, or\nboth.\n\"(5C) Subsection (5A) does not prevent a cash dealer from\ncommunicating or disclosing to any court any information, or\nmatter, referred to in that subsection.\"."
    },
