    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 After section 28 of the Principal Act the following section is",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"28A. (1) ^Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n28 (2), extend the period of effect of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 27 (1), (2) and (3) apply, with the necessary changes\nmade, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining order\nmade in reliance on subsection 28 (2) in the same way as they apply to\nthe making of a restraining order.\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of the period of effect of a restraining\norder to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional",
      "skos:definition": "inserted:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"28A. (1) ^Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n28 (2), extend the period of effect of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 27 (1), (2) and (3) apply, with the necessary changes\nmade, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining order\nmade in reliance on subsection 28 (2) in the same way as they apply to\nthe making of a restraining order.\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of the period of effect of a restraining\norder to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-26-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-26-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55940dd3679b9a68b1dfef2a56b01b00cde6e62dc278233fa5829f1575870496",
      "skos:note": "The court may extend the period of effect of a restraining order on application by the DPP."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 After section 28 of the Principal Act the following section is",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "inserted:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nExtension of certain restraining orders\n\"28A. (1) ^Subject to subsection (2), the court may, on application\nmade by the DPP before the end of the period mentioned in subsection\n28 (2), extend the period of effect of a restraining order made in\nreliance on that subsection.\n\"(2) Subsections 27 (1), (2) and (3) apply, with the necessary changes\nmade, to the extension of the period of operation of a restraining order\nmade in reliance on subsection 28 (2) in the same way as they apply to\nthe making of a restraining order.\n\"(3) The DPP must give written notice of an application under\nsubsection ( 1 ) for the extension of the period of effect of a restraining\norder to:\n(a) the owner of the property against which the restraining order\nwas made; and\n(b) any other person who the DPP has reason to believe may have\nan interest in the property.\".\nTransitional"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-26-norm",
