    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Section 28",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-28"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 32 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nparagraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the\nRegistrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in\nthis paragraph called the 'owner'); or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of any\nproperty) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or\nboth; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both—that person; and\".\n(2) The amendment made by subsection (1) applies in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 32 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nparagraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the\nRegistrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in\nthis paragraph called the 'owner'); or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of any\nproperty) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or\nboth; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both—that person; and\".\n(2) The amendment made by subsection (1) applies in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-28-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aeb9aa50207d3bc5fbb0c89d950d098ae3eda4d29911b1dde9c6d88db1a4583a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-28",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Section 28",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 32 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nparagraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the\nRegistrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in\nthis paragraph called the 'owner'); or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of any\nproperty) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or\nboth; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both—that person; and\".\n(2) The amendment made by subsection (1) applies in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection."
    },
    {
