      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 32 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nparagraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the\nRegistrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in\nthis paragraph called the 'owner'); or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of any\nproperty) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or\nboth; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both—that person; and\".",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 32 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nparagraph (1) (c) and substituting the following paragraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or the\nRegistrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner of property subject to the restraining order (in\nthis paragraph called the 'owner'); or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of any\nproperty) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the defendant, or\nboth; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both—that person; and\".",
      "values:partOf": {
