    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-31",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "31 Section 31",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-31"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 243F of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting before subsection (1) the following subsection:\n\"(lAA) In this section:\n'defendant' has the same meaning as in section 243E.\";\n(b) by omitting subparagraph (l)(d)(ii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraphs:\n\"(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant; or\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—a\ndirector of the body corporate specified by the Court;\";\n(c) by inserting in paragraph (l)(d) \"or defendant\" after \"owner\"\n(last occurring);\n(d) by omitting paragraph ( 1 ) (e) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(e) for the examination on oath before the Court or Registrar\nof the Court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor defendant, or both—that person;\";\n(e) by adding at the end the following subsection:\n\"(5) In proceedings dealing with an application for an order\nunder subsection (1), a witness is not required to answer a\nquestion or to produce a document if the Court is satisfied that\nthe answering of the question or the production of the document\nmay prejudice the investigation of, or the prosecution of a\nperson for, an offence.\".\n(2) The amendments made by paragraphs (l)(a), (b), (c) and (d)\napply in relation to restraining orders made before or after the\ncommencement of this section.\n(3) The amendment made by paragraph ( 1 ) (e) applies in relation\nto a witness appearing after the commencement of this section in\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nproceedings dealing with an application for an order under subsection\n243F(1), whenever made, in relation to a restraining order existing at,\nor made after, that commencement.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 243F of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting before subsection (1) the following subsection:\n\"(lAA) In this section:\n'defendant' has the same meaning as in section 243E.\";\n(b) by omitting subparagraph (l)(d)(ii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraphs:\n\"(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant; or\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—a\ndirector of the body corporate specified by the Court;\";\n(c) by inserting in paragraph (l)(d) \"or defendant\" after \"owner\"\n(last occurring);\n(d) by omitting paragraph ( 1 ) (e) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(e) for the examination on oath before the Court or Registrar\nof the Court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor defendant, or both—that person;\";\n(e) by adding at the end the following subsection:\n\"(5) In proceedings dealing with an application for an order\nunder subsection (1), a witness is not required to answer a\nquestion or to produce a document if the Court is satisfied that\nthe answering of the question or the production of the document\nmay prejudice the investigation of, or the prosecution of a\nperson for, an offence.\".\n(2) The amendments made by paragraphs (l)(a), (b), (c) and (d)\napply in relation to restraining orders made before or after the\ncommencement of this section.\n(3) The amendment made by paragraph ( 1 ) (e) applies in relation\nto a witness appearing after the commencement of this section in\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nproceedings dealing with an application for an order under subsection\n243F(1), whenever made, in relation to a restraining order existing at,\nor made after, that commencement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-31-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-31-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-31-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fd4bb65b93fe24b43fabee04c5926ab6c95bd9ffb1386e828cc7454ed7b5d3dd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-31",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "31 Section 31",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 243F of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting before subsection (1) the following subsection:\n\"(lAA) In this section:\n'defendant' has the same meaning as in section 243E.\";\n(b) by omitting subparagraph (l)(d)(ii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraphs:\n\"(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant; or\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—a\ndirector of the body corporate specified by the Court;\";\n(c) by inserting in paragraph (l)(d) \"or defendant\" after \"owner\"\n(last occurring);\n(d) by omitting paragraph ( 1 ) (e) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(e) for the examination on oath before the Court or Registrar\nof the Court of any person, including:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) the defendant;\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor defendant, or both—that person;\";\n(e) by adding at the end the following subsection:\n\"(5) In proceedings dealing with an application for an order\nunder subsection (1), a witness is not required to answer a\nquestion or to produce a document if the Court is satisfied that\nthe answering of the question or the production of the document\nmay prejudice the investigation of, or the prosecution of a\nperson for, an offence.\".\n(2) The amendments made by paragraphs (l)(a), (b), (c) and (d)\napply in relation to restraining orders made before or after the\ncommencement of this section.\n(3) The amendment made by paragraph ( 1 ) (e) applies in relation\nto a witness appearing after the commencement of this section in\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nproceedings dealing with an application for an order under subsection\n243F(1), whenever made, in relation to a restraining order existing at,\nor made after, that commencement."
    },
