    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-34",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34 After Part VI of the Principal Act the following Part is inserted:",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-34"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "\"PART VIA—CTR INFORMATION\nRequests for CTR information\n\"37A. (1) Where a foreign country, being a country to which this\nAct applies because of regulations made under subsection 7 (2A), asks\nthe Attorney-General to give information to it, the Attorney-General\nmay direct the Director of the Cash Transaction Reports Agency to\ngive the Attorney-General access to such of the information requested\nas is CTR information, for the purpose of enabling the AttorneyGeneral to deal with the request.\n\"(2) In this section:\n'CTR information' has the same meaning as in the Cash Transaction\nReports Act 1988.\".\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991",
      "skos:definition": "\"PART VIA—CTR INFORMATION\nRequests for CTR information\n\"37A. (1) Where a foreign country, being a country to which this\nAct applies because of regulations made under subsection 7 (2A), asks\nthe Attorney-General to give information to it, the Attorney-General\nmay direct the Director of the Cash Transaction Reports Agency to\ngive the Attorney-General access to such of the information requested\nas is CTR information, for the purpose of enabling the AttorneyGeneral to deal with the request.\n\"(2) In this section:\n'CTR information' has the same meaning as in the Cash Transaction\nReports Act 1988.\".\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-34-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-34-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d73e59ac9371bf3a8e50c7b6a38a555852d3a3801d6a02f3e6bc108b6a992da2",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General may direct Director of Cash Transaction Reports Agency to provide CTR information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-34",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34 After Part VI of the Principal Act the following Part is inserted:",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "\"PART VIA—CTR INFORMATION\nRequests for CTR information\n\"37A. (1) Where a foreign country, being a country to which this\nAct applies because of regulations made under subsection 7 (2A), asks\nthe Attorney-General to give information to it, the Attorney-General\nmay direct the Director of the Cash Transaction Reports Agency to\ngive the Attorney-General access to such of the information requested\nas is CTR information, for the purpose of enabling the AttorneyGeneral to deal with the request.\n\"(2) In this section:\n'CTR information' has the same meaning as in the Cash Transaction\nReports Act 1988.\".\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991"
    },
