      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "Section 7 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nsubparagraph (8) (b) (ii) and substituting the following subparagraph:\n\"(ii) the Minister of the Crown of each participating State who is\nresponsible for:\n(A) if the State has no Police Force—police affairs in that\nState; and\n(B) in every other case—matters relating to the Police Force\nof that State;\".",
      "skos:definition": "Section 7 of the Principal Act is amended by omitting\nsubparagraph (8) (b) (ii) and substituting the following subparagraph:\n\"(ii) the Minister of the Crown of each participating State who is\nresponsible for:\n(A) if the State has no Police Force—police affairs in that\nState; and\n(B) in every other case—matters relating to the Police Force\nof that State;\".",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-37-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-37-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b09733c15a47b98ae0462d3199dabb62ab98341a6fd7f31abf78acc350b2b0cc",
      "skos:note": "The Minister of the Crown is responsible for police affairs in a State with no Police Force, and matters relating to the Police Force in other States."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-37",
