    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-48",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48 Section 48",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-48"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 48 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting paragraph (l)(c) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or\nthe registrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) a person whose property is the subject of the\nrestraining order (in this section called the 'owner');\nor\n(ii) a person who is the defendant within the meaning\nof section 43 in relation to the offence to which\nthe restraining order relates (in this subsection\ncalled the 'defendant');\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor the defendant or both—that person;\";\n(b) by inserting after paragraph (1) (d) the following paragraph:\n\"(da) an order directing:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant;\nor\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—\na director of the body corporate specified by the\ncourt;\nto give to:\n(iv) where the restraining order is, or includes, an order\nmade under paragraph 43 (2) (b)—the Official\nTrustee; and\n(v) in any other case—the applicant for the ancillary\norder or such other person as the court directs;\nwithin a period specified in the ancillary order, a\nstatement sworn on oath setting out such particulars of\nthe property, or dealings with the property, of the owner\nor the defendant, as the case may be, as the court thinks\nproper.\";\n(c) by omitting subparagraph (l)(e)(iii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraph:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(üi) an order directing the owner or another person to do any\nact or thing necessary or convenient to be done to enable\nthe Official Trustee to take custody and control of the\nproperty in accordance with the restraining order;\";\n(d) by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection:\n\"(2A) An ancillary\norder\nmade\nbefore\nor\nafter\nthe\ncommencement of this subsection in relation to a restraining\norder that is in force on or after that commencement does not\ncease to have effect merely because the restraining order, or\npart of it, ceases to be in force under paragraph 57 (2) (e) or\n(g).\";\n(e) by omitting from subsection (6A) \"subsection (1) directs to\nfurnish a statement to the Official Trustee\" and substituting\n\"paragraph (1) (da) directs to give a statement\";\n(f) by omitting from subsection (6A) \"furnishing\" and substituting\n\"giving\";\n(g) by omitting from subsection (6B) \"furnishes a statement to the\nOfficial Trustee\" and substituting \"gives a statement\";\n(h) by omitting from subsection (6B) \"subsection (1)\" and\nsubstituting \"paragraph (l)(f)\".\n(2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.\nWhen restraining order ceases to be in force",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 48 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting paragraph (l)(c) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or\nthe registrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) a person whose property is the subject of the\nrestraining order (in this section called the 'owner');\nor\n(ii) a person who is the defendant within the meaning\nof section 43 in relation to the offence to which\nthe restraining order relates (in this subsection\ncalled the 'defendant');\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor the defendant or both—that person;\";\n(b) by inserting after paragraph (1) (d) the following paragraph:\n\"(da) an order directing:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant;\nor\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—\na director of the body corporate specified by the\ncourt;\nto give to:\n(iv) where the restraining order is, or includes, an order\nmade under paragraph 43 (2) (b)—the Official\nTrustee; and\n(v) in any other case—the applicant for the ancillary\norder or such other person as the court directs;\nwithin a period specified in the ancillary order, a\nstatement sworn on oath setting out such particulars of\nthe property, or dealings with the property, of the owner\nor the defendant, as the case may be, as the court thinks\nproper.\";\n(c) by omitting subparagraph (l)(e)(iii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraph:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(üi) an order directing the owner or another person to do any\nact or thing necessary or convenient to be done to enable\nthe Official Trustee to take custody and control of the\nproperty in accordance with the restraining order;\";\n(d) by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection:\n\"(2A) An ancillary\norder\nmade\nbefore\nor\nafter\nthe\ncomm",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-48-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-48-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "741d56a1e4ba335da404c0cf19e471f3fcb5a153da2cde6957c96a4e0abf1540"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-48",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48 Section 48",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 19,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 48 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting paragraph (l)(c) and substituting the following\nparagraph:\n\"(c) an order for the examination on oath before the court or\nthe registrar of the court of any person, including:\n(i) a person whose property is the subject of the\nrestraining order (in this section called the 'owner');\nor\n(ii) a person who is the defendant within the meaning\nof section 43 in relation to the offence to which\nthe restraining order relates (in this subsection\ncalled the 'defendant');\nabout the affairs (including the nature and location of\nany property) of:\n(iii) anyone else who is either the owner or the\ndefendant, or both; and\n(iv) if the person to be examined is either the owner\nor the defendant or both—that person;\";\n(b) by inserting after paragraph (1) (d) the following paragraph:\n\"(da) an order directing:\n(i) the owner; or\n(ii) if the owner is not the defendant—the defendant;\nor\n(iii) if the owner or the defendant is a body corporate—\na director of the body corporate specified by the\ncourt;\nto give to:\n(iv) where the restraining order is, or includes, an order\nmade under paragraph 43 (2) (b)—the Official\nTrustee; and\n(v) in any other case—the applicant for the ancillary\norder or such other person as the court directs;\nwithin a period specified in the ancillary order, a\nstatement sworn on oath setting out such particulars of\nthe property, or dealings with the property, of the owner\nor the defendant, as the case may be, as the court thinks\nproper.\";\n(c) by omitting subparagraph (l)(e)(iii) and substituting the\nfollowing subparagraph:\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\n\"(üi) an order directing the owner or another person to do any\nact or thing necessary or convenient to be done to enable\nthe Official Trustee to take custody and control of the\nproperty in accordance with the restraining order;\";\n(d) by inserting after subsection (2) the following subsection:\n\"(2A) An ancillary\norder\nmade\nbefore\nor\nafter\nthe\ncommencement of this subsection in relation to a restraining\norder that is in force on or after that commencement does not\ncease to have effect merely because the restraining order, or\npart of it, ceases to be in force under paragraph 57 (2) (e) or\n(g).\";\n(e) by omitting from subsection (6A) \"subsection (1) directs to\nfurnish a statement to the Official Trustee\" and substituting\n\"paragraph (1) (da) directs to give a statement\";\n(f) by omitting from subsection (6A) \"furnishing\" and substituting\n\"giving\";\n(g) by omitting from subsection (6B) \"furnishes a statement to the\nOfficial Trustee\" and substituting \"gives a statement\";\n(h) by omitting from subsection (6B) \"subsection (1)\" and\nsubstituting \"paragraph (l)(f)\".\n(2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.\nWhen restraining order ceases to be in force"
    },
