    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-49",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49 Section 49",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-49"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 57 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting in subparagraph (2) (e) (i) \"that is a pecuniary\npenalty order\" after \"confiscation order\";\n(b) by omitting from subparagraph (2) (e) (ii) \"confiscation order\"\nand substituting \"pecuniary penalty order\";\n(c) by omitting from paragraph (2) (e) \"when the confiscation order\nis satisfied or otherwise ceases to be in force\" and substituting\n\", upon the pecuniary penalty order being satisfied or otherwise\nceasing to be in force, to the extent that the property to which\nthe restraining order relates is the same as the property that is\nsold or otherwise disposed of to satisfy the pecuniary penalty\norder and pay the costs, charges, expenses and remuneration\nreferred to in subsection 49 (6)\";\n(d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (g) \"19 or\" after \"section\".\n(2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nProduction orders",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 57 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by inserting in subparagraph (2) (e) (i) \"that is a pecuniary\npenalty order\" after \"confiscation order\";\n(b) by omitting from subparagraph (2) (e) (ii) \"confiscation order\"\nand substituting \"pecuniary penalty order\";\n(c) by omitting from paragraph (2) (e) \"when the confiscation order\nis satisfied or otherwise ceases to be in force\" and substituting\n\", upon the pecuniary penalty order being satisfied or otherwise\nceasing to be in force, to the extent that the property to which\nthe restraining order relates is the same as the property that is\nsold or otherwise disposed of to satisfy the pecuniary penalty\norder and pay the costs, charges, expenses and remuneration\nreferred to in subsection 49 (6)\";\n(d) by inserting in paragraph (2) (g) \"19 or\" after \"section\".\n(2) The amendments made by subsection (1) apply in relation to\nrestraining orders made before or after the commencement of this\nsection.\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2)\nNo. 123, 1991\nProduction orders",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-49-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-49-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ebc54048cf2b016daf885a03b24131b32520795ec0b80f9f6c5628930eecace1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-act#sec-49",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
